From: Khem Raj <raj.khem@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] g2d_utils: Store strtol() result in a long

getSystemEnvInt() assigns the result of strtol() to an int and then
compares it with LONG_MAX/LONG_MIN. On LP64 targets the value is
truncated before the comparison, so the ERANGE overflow check can never
trigger. Clang diagnoses this:

  os/linux/g2d_utils.c:33:31: error: result of comparison of constant
  9223372036854775807 with expression of type 'int' is always false
  [-Werror,-Wtautological-constant-out-of-range-compare]

Keep the value in a long, reject values that do not fit in an int, and
narrow explicitly on return.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Khem Raj <raj.khem@gmail.com>
---
 source/os/linux/g2d_utils.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/source/os/linux/g2d_utils.c b/source/os/linux/g2d_utils.c
index 1321f8a..c6079da 100644
--- a/source/os/linux/g2d_utils.c
+++ b/source/os/linux/g2d_utils.c
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@ enum g2d_ocl_enabled { G2D_OCL_UNKNOWN, G2D_OCL_ENABLED, G2D_OCL_DISABLED };
 static atomic_int g_g2d_ocl_status = G2D_OCL_UNKNOWN;
 static int getSystemEnvInt(char *prop)
 {
-	int val;
+	long val;
 #ifdef ANDROID
 	char env[PROPERTY_VALUE_MAX];
 	property_get("vendor.2d.ocl.enable", env, "1");
@@ -31,10 +31,11 @@ static int getSystemEnvInt(char *prop)
 	errno = 0; /* To distinguish success/failure after call */
 	val = strtol(env, NULL, 10);
 	if ((errno == ERANGE && (val == LONG_MAX || val == LONG_MIN))
-			|| (errno != 0 && val == 0)) {
+			|| (errno != 0 && val == 0)
+			|| val > INT_MAX || val < INT_MIN) {
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
-	return val;
+	return (int)val;
 }
 
 int isOCLEnabled()
